+### November 5, 2026
+
+- You can now set up an IP allowlist for your organization in the Claude Console, in beta. Requests to covered services from addresses not on your list are refused, which limits where a leaked API key can be used. Add IPv4 and IPv6 addresses or CIDR ranges, up to 1,000 per organization. See IP allowlisting for what's covered and how to set it up.
+- You can now sign a member of your Claude Enterprise (claude.ai) organization out of Claude everywhere with the Admin API (see the Admin API reference). `POST /v1/organizations/users/{user_id}/sign_out` is in beta, and every request must include the `admin-user-sign-out-2026-10-08` beta header. It ends the member's sign-in sessions and trusted devices on every browser and device, and their OAuth tokens for your organization. The member stays in the organization and can sign in again right away. See Sign a member out everywhere for the key scope that the request needs and for what it doesn't end.
+
+### November 3, 2026
+
+- Text generated by Claude Mythos 5, Claude Opus 4.7, and Claude Sonnet 4.6 carries Anthropic's text watermark on the platforms listed in How Claude marks AI-generated content. On Claude Sonnet 4.6, text generated for a request that sets `temperature`, `top_p`, or `top_k` to a non-default value might not carry it. See Text watermark.
+
+### November 2, 2026
+
+- Long conversations and agent loops on the Messages API can now send smaller requests and get a lower time to first token with message threads, in beta with the `message-threads-2026-08-12` beta header. The API keeps the conversation on the server, so each later request sends only the new messages. A thread expires 5 minutes after its last request and is deleted no more than 1 hour after its last use. Message threads are available on the Claude API, Claude Platform on AWS, Claude Models on Google Cloud (Anthropic managed), and Claude in Microsoft Foundry.
+
+### October 30, 2026
+
+- We've deprecated fast mode for Claude Opus 4.8, with removal on November 30, 2026. After removal, requests to `claude-opus-4-8` with `speed: "fast"` will return an error. To continue using fast mode, migrate to Claude Opus 5.5. Read more in Fast mode model availability.
+
+### October 29, 2026
+
+- We've launched the Usage and Cost Analytics API in beta with the `analytics-usage-cost-2026-08-24` beta header. Its `/v1/organizations/analytics/usage` and `/v1/organizations/analytics/cost` endpoints report token usage and cost for Claude Console and Claude Enterprise organizations. You can filter and group results by dimensions such as model, workspace, API key, and the user or service account behind each request.
+- The Usage and Cost API is now a legacy API, and so are the `usage_report`, `cost_report`, `user_usage_report`, and `user_cost_report` endpoints of the Claude Enterprise Analytics API. All of them remain supported. To move an existing integration, see Migrate from the Usage and Cost API or Migrate from the Claude Enterprise usage and cost reports.
+
+### October 28, 2026
+
+- We've raised the maximum request size for the Messages API and the Token Counting API from 32 MB to 128 MB on the first-party Claude API.
+
